      <title>WOMEN, POWER, AND PUBLIC LEADERSHIP: A Fireside Chat on What Global Leadership Requires in Uncertain Times at Founders Library</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/53761774454560/huge/a4e9360806bbb7273380b6b56895d4b2ec82053e.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Tue, 25 Aug 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>Join the Center for Women, Gender, and Global Leadership for a special fireside chat featuring Her Excellency Paula-Mae Weekes, former President of the Republic of Trinidad and Tobago and the first woman to serve as President of Trinidad and Tobago.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Moderated by Professor J. Jarpa Dawuni, the conversation will explore what global leadership requires in uncertain times, with a focus on women, power, and public leadership.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Tuesday, August 25 | 1:00-2:30 p.m.
<br>Reception to follow. </p>

<p> </p>

<p>RSVP Here: <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdY_epKfLhHFYotxcDryLLmjpCRy4hPm6aB5raAq1ef3UfZ9g/viewform">https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdY_epKfLhHFYotxcDryLLmjpCRy4hPm6aB5raAq1ef3UfZ9g/viewform</a></p>

